12. Minimum and Maximum Selection Rules
    Explain:

- Minimum selected sequences depend on workflow
- Typical transfer workflow requires at least:
  - Tip pick up sequence
  - Aspirate/source sequence
  - Dispense/target sequence
- Tip eject may be included when available
- Multiple sequences can be selected when method uses multiple transfer blocks, variants, or repeated processes
- Users must not leave required step roles undefined
- If DevPal cannot detect transfer type or required context, it should ask the user rather than assume

